text:
```yaml
design:
  schema: fpga-design-agent/project/v1
  name: vmed
  board: nexys_a7_100t
  clocks:
    - {name: clk_sys, source: board, port: CLK100MHZ, mhz: 100}
    - {name: clk_pix, source: mmcm, from: clk_sys, mhz: 74.25}
  resets:
    - {name: rst_pix, domain: clk_pix, polarity: active_high, style: sync, from: CPU_RESETN, via: reset_sync}
  shell: {design_id: VMED, clock: clk_pix, reset: rst_pix}
  modules:
    - name: video_source
      kind: rtl
      clocks: {clk: clk_pix}
      resets: {rst: rst_pix}
      window_base: 0x00
      register_crossings: {}
    - name: median_filter
      kind: rtl
      clocks: {clk: clk_pix}
      resets: {rst: rst_pix}
    - name: vga_output
      kind: rtl
      clocks: {clk: clk_pix}
      resets: {rst: rst_pix}
      window_base: 0x04
      register_crossings: {}
  connections:
    - {from: video_source.out, to: median_filter.in}
    - {from: median_filter.out, to: vga_output.in}
  board_ports:
    - {name: CLK100MHZ, dir: in, drive: input, to: clk_sys}
    - {name: CPU_RESETN, dir: in, drive: input, to: rst_pix}
    - {name: BTNC, dir: in, drive: input, to: video_source.button_center}
    - {name: UART_TXD_IN, dir: in, drive: input, to: shell.uart_rx}
    - {name: UART_RXD_OUT, dir: out, drive: push-pull, from: shell.uart_tx}
    - {name: VGA_R[3:0], dir: out, drive: push-pull, from: vga_output.vga_r}
    - {name: VGA_G[3:0], dir: out, drive: push-pull, from: vga_output.vga_g}
    - {name: VGA_B[3:0], dir: out, drive: push-pull, from: vga_output.vga_b}
    - {name: VGA_HS, dir: out, drive: push-pull, from: vga_output.vga_hs}
    - {name: VGA_VS, dir: out, drive: push-pull, from: vga_output.vga_vs}
    - {name: LED[0], dir: out, drive: push-pull, from: clk_pix.locked}
  owned: []
  assumptions:
    - id: A-1
      text: "The checkerboard pattern uses equal-sized black and white squares."
      default: "Use a 16 by 16 active-pixel square size, anchored at the top-left of the active picture."
      reason: "The specification requires a black-and-white checkerboard but does not specify its square size."
      affects: [video_source.pattern]
      status: open
    - id: A-2
      text: "The test shell uses newline-terminated ASCII commands and responses."
      default: "Use 8N1; accept PATTERN BARS, PATTERN CHECKER, and FRAME?; respond with OK or a decimal frame count, followed by a newline."
      reason: "The UART framing and command syntax are not specified; this gives the host a simple way to select either pattern and read the counter."
      affects: [shell.design_id, video_source.contract.registers, vga_output.contract.registers]
      status: open
    - id: A-3
      text: "BTNC is pressed"
      default: "Treat a high BTNC level as pressed."
      reason: "The specification names the button but does not state its electrical polarity."
      affects: [video_source.contract.ports.button_center]
      status: open
    - id: A-4
      text: "the pixel clock is not stable"
      default: "Hold the pixel-domain pipeline in reset and blank its outputs until the MMCM is locked; assert reset again if lock is lost."
      reason: "The specification requires black output while the pixel clock is unstable but does not specify reset or lock sequencing."
      affects: [clk_pix, rst_pix, vga_output.contract.ports.vga_r, vga_output.contract.ports.vga_g, vga_output.contract.ports.vga_b]
      status: open

contracts:
  video_source:
    schema: fpga-design-agent/contract/v1
    module: video_source
    summary: "Generates a continuous 720p raster and selectable test pattern, including raster metadata."
    parameters: []
    clocks:
      - {name: clk, port: clk, max_mhz: 74.25}
    resets:
      - {name: rst, port: rst, clock: clk, polarity: active_high, style: sync}
    ports:
      - {name: clk, dir: in}
      - {name: rst, dir: in}
      - {name: button_center, dir: in, width: 1, clock: clk}
      - {name: pattern, dir: in, width: 1, clock: clk}
      - {name: m_axis_tvalid, dir: out, clock: clk, reset_value: 0}
      - {name: m_axis_tready, dir: in, clock: clk}
      - {name: m_axis_tdata, dir: out, width: 33, clock: clk, reset_value: 0}
      - {name: m_axis_tuser, dir: out, width: 4, clock: clk, reset_value: 0}
      - {name: m_axis_tlast, dir: out, clock: clk, reset_value: 0}
    data_formats:
      - {name: x_coord, format: u11, packing: "Horizontal raster coordinate, 0 through 1649."}
      - {name: y_coord, format: u10, packing: "Vertical raster coordinate, 0 through 749."}
      - {name: rgb444, format: u12, packing: "R[3:0], G[3:0], B[3:0], with each channel 0xF when on and 0x0 when off."}
    interfaces:
      - name: out
        protocol: axi4-stream
        role: master
        prefix: m_axis
        clock: clk
        reset: rst
        tdata:
          width: 33
          fields:
            - {name: x, bits: [32, 22], format: x_coord}
            - {name: y, bits: [21, 12], format: y_coord}
            - {name: rgb, bits: [11, 0], format: rgb444}
        tuser:
          - {bit: 0, name: active, meaning: "1 during the 1280 by 720 active picture"}
          - {bit: 1, name: hsync, meaning: "Positive horizontal sync"}
          - {bit: 2, name: vsync, meaning: "Positive vertical sync"}
          - {bit: 3, name: force_blank, meaning: "1 while BTNC is pressed"}
        tlast: "End of each 1650-pixel line."
        packet_beats: 1650
        backpressure: false
        source_gaps: false
    registers:
      bus: top
      map:
        - name: PATTERN
          offset: 0x00
          access: RW
          reset: 0
          width: 1
          volatile: false
          fields:
            - {name: pattern, bits: [0, 0], port: pattern}
    throughput:
      - {interface: out, beats_per_cycle: 1}

  median_filter:
    schema: fpga-design-agent/contract/v1
    module: median_filter
    summary: "Produces the per-channel 3 by 3 median for each active pixel and delays raster metadata to keep it aligned."
    parameters: []
    clocks:
      - {name: clk, port: clk, max_mhz: 74.25}
    resets:
      - {name: rst, port: rst, clock: clk, polarity: active_high, style: sync}
    ports:
      - {name: clk, dir: in}
      - {name: rst, dir: in}
      - {name: s_axis_tvalid, dir: in, clock: clk}
      - {name: s_axis_tready, dir: out, clock: clk, reset_value: 0}
      - {name: s_axis_tdata, dir: in, width: 33, clock: clk}
      - {name: s_axis_tuser, dir: in, width: 4, clock: clk}
      - {name: s_axis_tlast, dir: in, clock: clk}
      - {name: m_axis_tvalid, dir: out, clock: clk, reset_value: 0}
      - {name: m_axis_tready, dir: in, clock: clk}
      - {name: m_axis_tdata, dir: out, width: 33, clock: clk, reset_value: 0}
      - {name: m_axis_tuser, dir: out, width: 4, clock: clk, reset_value: 0}
      - {name: m_axis_tlast, dir: out, clock: clk, reset_value: 0}
    data_formats:
      - {name: x_coord, format: u11, packing: "Horizontal raster coordinate, 0 through 1649."}
      - {name: y_coord, format: u10, packing: "Vertical raster coordinate, 0 through 749."}
      - {name: rgb444, format: u12, packing: "R[3:0], G[3:0], B[3:0], with each channel 0xF when on and 0x0 when off."}
    interfaces:
      - name: in
        protocol: axi4-stream
        role: slave
        prefix: s_axis
        clock: clk
        reset: rst
        tdata:
          width: 33
          fields:
            - {name: x, bits: [32, 22], format: x_coord}
            - {name: y, bits: [21, 12], format: y_coord}
            - {name: rgb, bits: [11, 0], format: rgb444}
        tuser:
          - {bit: 0, name: active, meaning: "1 during the 1280 by 720 active picture"}
          - {bit: 1, name: hsync, meaning: "Positive horizontal sync"}
          - {bit: 2, name: vsync, meaning: "Positive vertical sync"}
          - {bit: 3, name: force_blank, meaning: "1 while BTNC is pressed"}
        tlast: "End of each 1650-pixel line."
        packet_beats: 1650
        backpressure: false
        source_gaps: false
      - name: out
        protocol: axi4-stream
        role: master
        prefix: m_axis
        clock: clk
        reset: rst
        tdata:
          width: 33
          fields:
            - {name: x, bits: [32, 22], format: x_coord}
            - {name: y, bits: [21, 12], format: y_coord}
            - {name: rgb, bits: [11, 0], format: rgb444}
        tuser:
          - {bit: 0, name: active, meaning: "1 during the 1280 by 720 active picture"}
          - {bit: 1, name: hsync, meaning: "Positive horizontal sync"}
          - {bit: 2, name: vsync, meaning: "Positive vertical sync"}
          - {bit: 3, name: force_blank, meaning: "1 while BTNC is pressed"}
        tlast: "End of each 1650-pixel line."
        packet_beats: 1650
        backpressure: false
        source_gaps: false
    latency:
      - {from: in, to: out, cycles: 1651}
    throughput:
      - {interface: in, beats_per_cycle: 1}
      - {interface: out, beats_per_cycle: 1}

  vga_output:
    schema: fpga-design-agent/contract/v1
    module: vga_output
    summary: "Drives VGA RGB and sync from the filtered raster and counts completed frames."
    parameters: []
    clocks:
      - {name: clk, port: clk, max_mhz: 74.25}
    resets:
      - {name: rst, port: rst, clock: clk, polarity: active_high, style: sync}
    ports:
      - {name: clk, dir: in}
      - {name: rst, dir: in}
      - {name: s_axis_tvalid, dir: in, clock: clk}
      - {name: s_axis_tready, dir: out, clock: clk, reset_value: 0}
      - {name: s_axis_tdata, dir: in, width: 33, clock: clk}
      - {name: s_axis_tuser, dir: in, width: 4, clock: clk}
      - {name: s_axis_tlast, dir: in, clock: clk}
      - {name: vga_r, dir: out, width: 4, clock: clk, reset_value: 0}
      - {name: vga_g, dir: out, width: 4, clock: clk, reset_value: 0}
      - {name: vga_b, dir: out, width: 4, clock: clk, reset_value: 0}
      - {name: vga_hs, dir: out, width: 1, clock: clk, reset_value: 0}
      - {name: vga_vs, dir: out, width: 1, clock: clk, reset_value: 0}
      - {name: frame_count, dir: out, width: 32, clock: clk, reset_value: 0}
    data_formats:
      - {name: x_coord, format: u11, packing: "Horizontal raster coordinate, 0 through 1649."}
      - {name: y_coord, format: u10, packing: "Vertical raster coordinate, 0 through 749."}
      - {name: rgb444, format: u12, packing: "R[3:0], G[3:0], B[3:0], with each channel 0xF when on and 0x0 when off."}
      - {name: frame_counter, format: u32, packing: "Completed-frame count, modulo 2^32."}
    interfaces:
      - name: in
        protocol: axi4-stream
        role: slave
        prefix: s_axis
        clock: clk
        reset: rst
        tdata:
          width: 33
          fields:
            - {name: x, bits: [32, 22], format: x_coord}
            - {name: y, bits: [21, 12], format: y_coord}
            - {name: rgb, bits: [11, 0], format: rgb444}
        tuser:
          - {bit: 0, name: active, meaning: "1 during the 1280 by 720 active picture"}
          - {bit: 1, name: hsync, meaning: "Positive horizontal sync"}
          - {bit: 2, name: vsync, meaning: "Positive vertical sync"}
          - {bit: 3, name: force_blank, meaning: "1 while BTNC is pressed"}
        tlast: "End of each 1650-pixel line."
        packet_beats: 1650
        backpressure: false
        source_gaps: false
    registers:
      bus: top
      map:
        - name: FRAME_COUNT
          offset: 0x00
          access: RO
          reset: 0
          width: 32
          volatile: true
          fields:
            - {name: frame_count, bits: [31, 0], port: frame_count}
    throughput:
      - {interface: in, beats_per_cycle: 1}

module_specs:
  video_source: |
    Generate one raster beat per pixel-clock cycle. Use 1650 clocks per line and 750 lines per frame, marking active video, positive syncs, and line ends in stream metadata. Pattern register value 0 selects the eight specified colour bars; value 1 selects the proposed black-and-white checkerboard. Carry BTNC as a force-blank flag in the stream.
  median_filter: |
    For every active output pixel, calculate the median of each colour channel independently from its 3 by 3 neighbourhood. Clamp neighbourhood coordinates to the nearest active-picture edge. Delay the pixel and its raster metadata equally so the filtered picture and syncs retain their positions.
  vga_output: |
    Drive the VGA channels from the filtered stream, outputting zero RGB outside active video, when force_blank is asserted, or while the pixel clock is unstable. Preserve the stream's positive syncs. Increment the 32-bit frame counter once per completed frame, modulo 2^32, and expose it in the top register window.
  shell: |
    The always-present fpga_shell owns the USB-UART and register window at 0x80-0xFF. Use the proposed 115200-baud, 8N1 newline-terminated ASCII command set to select a pattern and read the frame counter. The shell identifies the design as VMED.

requirements:
  - id: S-1
    text: "Generate 1280 x 720 active video at 60 Hz using a 74.25 MHz pixel clock, 1650 pixel clocks per line (1280 active, 110 front porch, 40 sync, 220 back porch), 750 lines per frame (720 active, 5 front porch, 5 sync, 20 back porch), and positive horizontal and vertical sync."
    proof: [simulation, hardware, analysis]
    modules: [video_source, median_filter, vga_output, top]
  - id: S-2
    text: "By default, generate eight vertical colour bars, each 160 active pixels wide, in this order: white, yellow, cyan, green, magenta, red, blue, black."
    proof: [simulation, hardware]
    modules: [video_source, top]
  - id: S-3
    text: "For each active output pixel, output the median of the nine samples in its 3 x 3 neighbourhood, computed independently for each colour channel."
    proof: [simulation, formal]
    modules: [median_filter, top]
  - id: S-4
    text: "Keep the output picture and horizontal and vertical sync aligned so each filtered output pixel occupies the same video position it would occupy without filtering."
    proof: [simulation, hardware]
    modules: [median_filter, vga_output, top]
  - id: S-5
    text: "Drive all colour outputs to zero outside the active picture, while BTNC is pressed, or while the pixel clock is not stable."
    proof: [simulation, hardware]
    modules: [video_source, vga_output, top]
  - id: S-6
    text: "Light LED[0] when the pixel clock is stable."
    proof: [simulation, hardware]
    modules: [top]
  - id: S-7
    text: "Provide a USB-UART test shell at 115200 baud that allows the host to choose the test pattern and read a frame counter; identify the design as VMED."
    proof: [simulation, hardware]
    modules: [video_source, vga_output, top]

