module_specs:
  video_source: |
    Generate one raster beat per pixel-clock cycle. Use 1650 clocks per line and 750 lines per frame, marking active video, positive syncs, and line ends in stream metadata. Pattern register value 0 selects the eight specified colour bars; value 1 selects the proposed black-and-white checkerboard. Carry BTNC as a force-blank flag in the stream.
  median_filter: |
    For every active output pixel, calculate the median of each colour channel independently from its 3 by 3 neighbourhood. Clamp neighbourhood coordinates to the nearest active-picture edge. Delay the pixel and its raster metadata equally so the filtered picture and syncs retain their positions.
  vga_output: |
    Drive the VGA channels from the filtered stream, outputting zero RGB outside active video, when force_blank is asserted, or while the pixel clock is unstable. Preserve the stream's positive syncs. Increment the 32-bit frame counter once per completed frame, modulo 2^32, and expose it in the top register window.
  shell: |
    The always-present fpga_shell owns the USB-UART and register window at 0x80-0xFF. Use the proposed 115200-baud, 8N1 newline-terminated ASCII command set to select a pattern and read the frame counter. The shell identifies the design as VMED.

requirements:
  - id: S-1
    text: "Generate 1280 x 720 active video at 60 Hz using a 74.25 MHz pixel clock, 1650 pixel clocks per line (1280 active, 110 front porch, 40 sync, 220 back porch), 750 lines per frame (720 active, 5 front porch, 5 sync, 20 back porch), and positive horizontal and vertical sync."
    proof: [simulation, hardware, analysis]
    modules: [video_source, median_filter, vga_output, top]
  - id: S-2
    text: "By default, generate eight vertical colour bars, each 160 active pixels wide, in this order: white, yellow, cyan, green, magenta, red, blue, black."
    proof: [simulation, hardware]
    modules: [video_source, top]
  - id: S-3
    text: "For each active output pixel, output the median of the nine samples in its 3 x 3 neighbourhood, computed independently for each colour channel."
    proof: [simulation, formal]
    modules: [median_filter, top]
  - id: S-4
    text: "Keep the output picture and horizontal and vertical sync aligned so each filtered output pixel occupies the same video position it would occupy without filtering."
    proof: [simulation, hardware]
    modules: [median_filter, vga_output, top]
  - id: S-5
    text: "Drive all colour outputs to zero outside the active picture, while BTNC is pressed, or while the pixel clock is not stable."
    proof: [simulation, hardware]
    modules: [video_source, vga_output, top]
  - id: S-6
    text: "Light LED[0] when the pixel clock is stable."
    proof: [simulation, hardware]
    modules: [top]
  - id: S-7
    text: "Provide a USB-UART test shell at 115200 baud that allows the host to choose the test pattern and read a frame counter; identify the design as VMED."
    proof: [simulation, hardware]
    modules: [video_source, vga_output, top]

